From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 15:01:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] add the vendored third-party licence texts to the wheel

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; the gap is present in every highspy wheel on PyPI, so it needs a maintainer discussion rather than a drive-by PR]

libhighs compiles three third-party components straight into the binary:
pdqsort (extern/pdqsort, zlib licence), zstr (extern/zstr, MIT) and the LP
file reader (highs/io/filereaderlp, MIT).  The MIT terms of the latter two
require the copyright notice to travel with binary redistributions, but the
wheel ships only LICENSE.txt and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, and the notices file
names the licences without reproducing them.

scikit-build-core copies exactly what project.license-files lists, preserving
each entry's path, so naming the three files is the whole change.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 pyproject.toml | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index 46ad827..953b53a 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -16,6 +16,9 @@ license = "MIT"
 license-files = [
   "LICENSE.txt",
   "THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md",
+  "extern/pdqsort/license.txt",
+  "extern/zstr/LICENSE",
+  "highs/io/filereaderlp/LICENSE",
 ]
 
 requires-python = ">=3.9"
